# Everyday chat short forms. They are English, not Hindi, and are never changed.
# short forms (comma separated) | what they stand for. A single-word meaning links them for prediction.
pls,plz,plss,plzz,pliz|please
u,yu|you
ur|your
tmrw,tmr|tomorrow
ok,okk,okkk,oki,okie,kk|okay
yup,yep,yess|yes
nope,noo|no
bcz,bcoz,coz,cuz,bcs|because
gud|good
mrng,mrnng|morning
nite|night
thnx,thx,thnks|thanks
lol,lolz|laugh out loud
omg,omfg|oh my god
btw|by the way
idk,idc|I do not know
brb|be right back
gm|good morning
gn|good night
tc|take care
fyi|for your information
asap|as soon as possible
ttyl|talk to you later
wfh|work from home
